---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Container from '../components/Container.astro';
import ballPit from '../assets/photos/ball-pit.jpg';

const refusals = [
  {
    lead: 'Scare you.',
    body: "Fear is the easiest way to get a parent's attention and about the worst way to actually help. There is already plenty of it going around. Your worries here are reasonable, and we are not going to farm them.",
  },
  {
    lead: 'Overstate the research.',
    body: 'Whether smartphones caused the rise in teenage anxiety is a live fight among serious researchers, and we say so on the pages where it comes up. The case for a more analog childhood does not need that argument, and a site that oversells its evidence deserves to be doubted on everything else.',
  },
  {
    lead: 'Tell you that you have already blown it.',
    body: 'Most people arrive here with devices in the house and habits already set. Every recommendation on this site has a first step that a family in exactly that position can take this week.',
  },
];
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="Why Offline Childhood exists, what we argue for, what we will not do, and how the site is paid for."
>
  <header class="border-b border-line bg-surface-2 py-14">
    <Container>
      <div class="grid items-center gap-x-12 gap-y-10 md:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1.15fr)_minmax(0,0.85fr)]">
        <div>
          <h1 class="text-balance font-display text-[clamp(36px,4vw,50px)] font-extrabold leading-[1.04] tracking-[-0.015em] text-navy">
            Why Offline Childhood?
          </h1>
          <p class="mt-6 max-w-[32em] text-[1.19rem] leading-[1.62] text-ink">
            We're parents, and we're trying. Trying to get outside more, delay the smartphone, keep
            dinner screen-free, and raise kids who can think for themselves about all of it.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-[240px_240px_24px_24px] bg-surface-3">
          <Image
            src={ballPit}
            alt="A young child seen from above, sitting in a ball pit of blue and green balls, holding a red cup."
            widths={[520, 1040]}
            sizes="(min-width: 768px) 480px, 92vw"
            class="h-[420px] w-full object-cover object-[30%_30%]"
          />
        </div>
      </div>
    </Container>
  </header>

  <div class="article-col pt-14">
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        We are not purists. Nobody here lives offline, and if you do, we salute you. What we think is
        that the culture has gotten badly out of hand on screen addiction, algorithmic feeds, and now
        AI, and that childhood is where that costs the most.
      </p>
      <p>
        So we argue for the analog side. More unstructured play, more paper, more time outdoors, more
        boredom. Not because technology is evil, but because an hour on a screen is an hour not
        spent on something else, and at this age the something else matters enormously.
      </p>

      <h2>Why we teach kids how the tech works too</h2>
      <p>
        Because they are going to use it. Probably in their careers, certainly for the rest of their
        lives. A kid who does not understand how an algorithm decides what she sees, or where an AI
        model got its material, or who is paying for the free app, has been left
        unprepared, however carefully she has been shielded.
      </p>
      <p>
        That is what the <a href="/conversations">Conversations</a> half of this site is for. Every
        idea is written four times over, for ages 4 to 6 through 13 and up, because a four-year-old
        can absolutely understand that a person chose what she is watching. Limits buy you the years
        in which understanding gets built. You need both.
      </p>

      <h2>What we will not do</h2>
    </div>

    {/* The refusals as the coral cross list rather than bold-led paragraphs. */}
    <ul class="mt-6 flex flex-col gap-0.5">
      {refusals.map((r) => (
        <li class="grid grid-cols-[30px_minmax(0,1fr)] gap-4 border-b border-line py-5">
          <span class="font-label text-xl font-bold leading-[1.3] text-coral" aria-hidden="true">&#10005;</span>
          <p class="text-[1.09rem] leading-[1.7] text-ink">
            <span class="font-display font-extrabold tracking-[-0.02em] text-navy">{r.lead}</span>{' '}
            {r.body}
          </p>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>

    <div class="prose mt-2">
      <h2>Who is it for?</h2>
      <p>
        Parents and caregivers. The advice leans younger, because that is where most of these
        decisions get made for the first time, but plenty of it works just as well with teenagers,
        and every conversation is written for older kids too. Teachers as well: they work with one
        kid at a dinner table or a class of thirty, and each one has a note on running it as a
        group.
      </p>

      <h2>How is it paid for?</h2>
      <p>
        It isn't. This site makes no money. Nothing is sponsored, no link pays us, and there is no
        advertising. Nobody can buy their way onto a page, and no company sees what we write before
        it goes up.
      </p>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-10 text-[0.94rem] leading-[1.7] text-ink-soft">
      The photographs are our own, except six from Unsplash: the forest path by{' '}
      <a href="https://unsplash.com/photos/u0vgcIOQG08" rel="noopener" target="_blank" class="underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-ink">Jens Lelie</a>, the
      speech bubble by{' '}
      <a href="https://unsplash.com/photos/V5vqWC9gyEU" rel="noopener" target="_blank" class="underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-ink">Volodymyr Hryshchenko</a>, the
      classroom by{' '}
      <a href="https://unsplash.com/photos/zFSo6bnZJTw" rel="noopener" target="_blank" class="underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-ink">Quilia</a>, the
      cafe by{' '}
      <a href="https://unsplash.com/photos/GiIZSko7Guk" rel="noopener" target="_blank" class="underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-ink">Bonnie Kittle</a>, the
      homework pair by{' '}
      <a href="https://unsplash.com/photos/sbHo9rRSIZc" rel="noopener" target="_blank" class="underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-ink">Vitaly Gariev</a>, and the
      street corner by{' '}
      <a href="https://unsplash.com/photos/FzYbSqjzmqM" rel="noopener" target="_blank" class="underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-ink">Andrei Shiptenko</a>.
    </p>

    <section class="mt-[72px] rounded-[28px] border-2 border-accent bg-panel-accent px-9 pb-[34px] pt-8">
      <h2 class="mb-3.5 font-display text-[26px] font-extrabold text-navy">Tell us what's missing</h2>
      <p class="text-[1.06rem] leading-[1.7] text-ink">
        Got a product or service we should look at? Know someone we should be reading? Came here for
        something and did not find it? Please tell us.{' '}
        <a href="mailto:hello@offlinechildhood.com" class="font-semibold text-primary-text underline underline-offset-4">
          hello@offlinechildhood.com
        </a>
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
